From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Keep the AF_UNIX reparse tag in file information.

AI-assisted (Codex), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted
upstream.

Windows 10 19045.6466 returns the AF_UNIX reparse tag from both
FileAttributeTagInfo and FileStatInformation on a bound socket file.
Wine v3 set the tag for sockets and then cleared it alongside the
default initialization. Set the default before populating attributes.

v4 (2026-11-18): Covers file information queried by handle. Keep the
existing mount-point and extended-attribute handling.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
@@ -1371,6 +1371,7 @@
     int attr_len, ret;
 
     *attr = 0;
+    if (reparse_tag) *reparse_tag = 0;
     ret = fstat( fd, st );
     if (ret == -1) return ret;
     *attr |= get_file_attributes( st );
@@ -1380,7 +1381,6 @@
         *attr |= FILE_ATTRIBUTE_REPARSE_POINT;
         if (reparse_tag) *reparse_tag = IO_REPARSE_TAG_AF_UNIX;
     }
-    if (reparse_tag) *reparse_tag = 0;
     /* consider mount points to be reparse points (IO_REPARSE_TAG_MOUNT_POINT) */
     if (options & FILE_OPEN_REPARSE_POINT)
     {
